  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a triathlon with a spreadsheet and zero rest days. By week six, the Achilles and shoulder had questions.\n\nThree sports mean three sets of loads stacking up. Running often accounts for the most injuries even with less training time, and bike-to-run sessions can be extra demanding on the calf and Achilles.\n\nWhat often helps: track your total load across all three sports and build running gently, do strength work for calves, hips and trunk twice a week, get a bike fit and work on swim technique, and schedule genuine rest days. If brick sessions bother your Achilles, shorten the run for a while.\n\nPain that persists or gets worse with training is worth getting assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
